  "claim": "The improvisational troupe, which trained Amy Sedaris, Paul Dinello, and Stephen Colber, was founded in 1959.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Exit 57. Sentence: Exit 57 is a 30-minute sketch comedy series that aired on the American television channel Comedy Central from 1995 to 1996; its cast was composed of comedians Amy Sedaris, Paul Dinello, Stephen Colbert, Jodi Lennon, and Mitch Rouse, all of whom had previously studied improv at The Second City in Chicago.\nPage: The Second City. Sentence: The Second City Theatre opened on December 16, 1959, and has since become one of the most influential and prolific comedy theatres in the world.",
